message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CG-SDL-AAF: A Reproducible Automated Assessment Framework for Self-Directed Learning in Computer Graphics"
abstract: "CG-SDL-AAF is an open-source, bilingual (Uzbek/English) framework for the automated assessment of self-directed work in computer graphics. It standardises student evidence (headless Blender re-rendering of .blend/.fbx scene files with a canonical camera and script execution disabled, helper-object filtering, automatic removal of the application interface from screenshots in dark and light themes, PCA+ICP pose alignment of meshes), compares it with a reference using perceptual image metrics in an object or a composition mode (foreground-weighted SSIM, MS-SSIM, CIEDE2000, edge F1, optional LPIPS) and geometric mesh metrics (Chamfer, Hausdorff, H95, F-score, topology relative to the reference), and returns a 0-100 score with formative feedback within a forethought-performance-self-reflection cycle. The release contains the desktop GUI, command-line interface, notebooks, tests, the technical-validation benchmark (development and held-out objects, feedback validation, sensitivity analysis) and the reference benchmark run reported in the accompanying manuscript."
